# gp-arb-bot — optional local configuration and secrets.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# Loaded by Node itself (`--env-file-if-exists`), so there is no dotenv dependency and no
# import to add. The launchd services pass this flag; running a script by hand does not,
# so for a manual run either export the vars or pass the flag yourself:
#
#   node --env-file-if-exists=.env scripts/watchdog.mjs
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Keep it 0600 — every other file this repo writes is readable by
# anyone on the machine, and this is the one that is not meant to be.
#
# NEVER put a secret in a launchd plist. Those live in ~/Library/LaunchAgents at mode 644,
# are readable by every account on the machine, and are captured by Time Machine long
# after the value is rotated. `lib/launchd.mjs` refuses to render one.

# ── Alerting (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The watchdog is INERT unless BOTH of these are set. Half-configured is reported once at
# startup rather than failing quietly, because "no alerts" and "alerting is broken" are
# otherwise the same observation.
#
# Bot token from @BotFather. Chat id from @userinfobot, or for a group, the `id` in
# https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates after posting a message there.
# A group/channel id is negative — keep the leading minus sign.
GPA_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
GPA_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── Everything below is optional; unset means the documented default ─────────
# Full table with ranges and rationale: CLAUDE.md §4.

# Which venues the watchdog monitors. Unset = auto-discover from the database, so a venue
# nobody runs is never alerted on. The installed plist pins this to `polymarket`.
# GPA_WATCH_VENUES=polymarket

# How often a NON-clearing set may be re-recorded, per event key (default 300000 = 5 min).
# Raising this cuts disk: the measured Polymarket write rate is ~0.3 GB/day at the default,
# ~0.1 GB/day at 15 min. Clears are ALWAYS written regardless.
# GPA_MISS_SAMPLE_MS=300000

# Retention for `opportunities`, swept hourly by the watchdog. 0 disables the sweep.
# GPA_KEEP_OPP_DAYS=90

# Per-venue feed staleness thresholds. Each MUST exceed GPA_MISS_SAMPLE_MS — a healthy but
# quiet feed writes nothing for one sampling period by design, so a lower threshold alerts
# on normal operation. Startup refuses the combination rather than letting it page you.
# GPA_FEED_STALE_MS_POLYMARKET=600000
# GPA_FEED_STALE_MS_KALSHI=1800000

# Dashboard. Loopback-only unless GPA_BIND is changed deliberately — nothing here is
# authenticated, so exposure should be a decision rather than an accident of a default.
# GPA_BIND=127.0.0.1
# GPA_PORT=4324
